# SPRINT 13 — REAL DURABLE POSTGRESQL PERSISTENCE

## OBJECTIVE

Implement a REAL durable PostgreSQL storage backend for AG-002 Memory Manager.

This sprint closes the biggest remaining production blocker identified by the final audit:

> "No real durable backend."

The existing storage abstraction, repository contracts, pagination, capabilities, idempotency, lifecycle, event log, cache, authorization, and security systems must be reused.

Do NOT redesign AG-002.

Do NOT rewrite existing memory services.

Do NOT introduce AG-003/AG-004.

Do NOT implement LLM/vector search.

Do NOT implement the production composition root yet.

This sprint is ONLY about real durable PostgreSQL persistence and the minimum repository/storage integration required to make it truthful.

==================================================
IMPORTANT ARCHITECTURAL RULE
============================

PostgreSQL must be a REAL backend.

Do NOT create:

* fake durable adapter
* in-memory fallback when durable is selected
* fake transaction implementation
* "durable" wrapper around InMemoryMemoryRepository
* mock persistence presented as production persistence

When:

MEMORY_STORAGE_BACKEND=durable

the system MUST actually use PostgreSQL.

If PostgreSQL configuration is missing or invalid:

FAIL CLOSED.

Do NOT silently fall back to memory.

The existing in-memory backend must remain available for tests/development.

