==================================================
PHASE 9 — TRANSACTIONS
======================

Implement REAL PostgreSQL transactions.

Do NOT claim ACID behavior for the in-memory backend.

For PostgreSQL:

transaction(callback)

must execute within a real database transaction.

Required behavior:

BEGIN
→ operations
→ COMMIT

On error:

BEGIN
→ operations
→ ROLLBACK

Test:

* successful transaction
* rollback on exception
* multiple operations
* visibility after commit
* absence after rollback

Do not expose raw database connections through public AG-002 APIs.

==================================================
PHASE 10 — CONCURRENCY & VERSION SAFETY
=======================================

Verify concurrent updates.

For versioned records:

Expected behavior:

read version N

update where:

id = X
AND version = N

then increment version.

If another writer already updated the record:

return the existing typed conflict error.

Do not silently overwrite.

Add tests for concurrent update races.

==================================================
PHASE 11 — IDEMPOTENT CREATE
============================

Sprint 10 implemented idempotent creation.

Ensure the PostgreSQL backend preserves:

same namespace + same key + identical logical input
→ safe retry / same logical record

Conflicting input:

same namespace + same key + different logical input
→ typed conflict

Different namespace:

same key
→ independent records

Concurrent identical creates:

→ exactly one logical record

No duplicate creation events.

Add PostgreSQL-specific concurrency tests.

==================================================
