======================================

Verify persistence of:

* Active
* Archived
* Expired
* Deleted
* Restored

Verify:

expiresAt survives restart.

Lifecycle evaluation must work after a process restart.

Do not rely on in-memory timers.

A record created with TTL must remain correctly represented in PostgreSQL.

After restart:

lifecycle evaluation must still identify expired records.

