==================================================
PHASE 14 — CACHE INTERACTION
============================

The cache remains in-memory.

That is acceptable.

When durable PostgreSQL is selected:

* cache reads may use memory cache
* database remains source of truth
* update invalidates cache
* archive invalidates cache
* restore invalidates cache
* expire invalidates cache
* erase invalidates cache

After process restart:

cache is empty
database remains authoritative

Do NOT attempt to make the cache durable in Sprint 13.

==================================================
PHASE 15 — DSR / ERASURE
========================

Verify Sprint 9 right-to-forget behavior against PostgreSQL.

eraseMemoryById:

must physically remove the record from PostgreSQL.

eraseMemoryByNamespace:

must remove all relevant records from PostgreSQL.

Verify:

* authorization
* namespace scope
* ownership
* clearance
* cache invalidation
* event tombstone
* replay semantics

After restart, erased memory MUST NOT reappear.

This is a critical persistence test.

